{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "tasks/a-task-s-line-gives-a-reason-of-the-closed-list-alone",
  "title": "A task's line gives why it did not complete from its terminal entry's task_end_reason when the closed list names it, by its code and in the runtime's words for each of the list's reasons; a reason off the list, or one that is no text, gives task_status and the turn's notes nothing of its own",
  "rules": [
    "§23.3 step 6",
    "§23.4"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-23.3-118",
    "RK-23.4-070",
    "RK-23.4-071"
  ],
  "notes": "Python: models/task.py TASK_END_WORDS and end_reason_fields, tasks/status.py _end_line, channels/_tasks_note.py _ending; tests/test_task_status.py::test_a_line_gives_a_reason_of_the_closed_list_alone. The entries are posted on the bus from outside the delegation, as another process or a host may: thirteen name each reason of the list, one a text off the list that reads as an instruction, one a list. task_status answers ten tasks at most and the notes list six, so the tasks are spread over two rooms; the reader's last two calls ask for the two tasks whose reason the list does not name, one at a time, and their answers hold no reason.",
